  "answer_text": "Officially, there is no permanent, 100% free, legal live video stream of the MSNBC TV channel available online without a paid TV subscription. Because MSNBC is a pay-TV cable network, the live broadcast is kept behind a digital paywall. \n\nHowever, there are several **legal and safe ways** to stream MSNBC live for free (either temporarily or through audio), as well as low-cost alternatives:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Best \"100% Free\" Option: Live Audio Streaming\nIf you only need to hear the news, commentary, and analysis, you can stream the live, real-time audio feed of MSNBC completely for free:\n* **TuneIn Radio:** You can listen to the live 24/7 MSNBC audio broadcast for free on the TuneIn website or via the TuneIn mobile app. \n* **MS NOW App:** The official MS NOW app allows users to listen to live audio of MSNBC's broadcasts for free without signing in.\n\n### 2. Free Trials of Live TV Streaming Services\nIf you want to watch the live video feed for a short period (such as during a major news event or election night), you can sign up for a free trial of an internet-based live TV provider. Just remember to cancel before the trial ends to avoid being charged:\n* **FuboTV:** Typically offers a **7-day free trial** and includes MSNBC in its base package.\n* **YouTube TV:** Usually offers a **7 to 14-day free trial** (promotions vary). It features high-quality streaming and unlimited DVR.\n* **DirecTV Stream:** Often offers a **5-day free trial** and carries MSNBC in its entry-level \"Entertainment\" package. \n\n### 3. Log in with a TV Provider (If You Have One)\nIf you, a family member, or a roommate already pay for a traditional cable, satellite, or live TV streaming subscription (like Sling, Hulu, or YouTube TV), you can watch for free:\n* Download the **MS NOW app** on your phone, tablet, or smart TV, or go to [NBC.com/live](https://www.nbc.com/live).\n* Select **MSNBC** and log in with your TV provider credentials to unlock the 24/7 live video stream.\n\n### 4. Watch Free Clips and Shows on Demand\nIf you do not need the continuous live channel but want to catch up on individual shows or segments:\n* **YouTube:** MSNBC uploads clips and full segments from major shows (like *The Rachel Maddow Show*, *The Beat with Ari Melber*, and *Morning Joe*) shortly after they air on their official [MSNBC YouTube Channel](https://www.youtube.com/@msnbc).\n* **MSNBC.com:** The official website hosts a large library of recent show segments and breaking news clips that are free to watch.\n\n---\n\n### Low-Cost / Alternative Options\n* **Sling TV (Sling Blue):** If you decide you want to pay for MSNBC without a heavy cable bill, Sling Blue is usually the cheapest live TV option (starting around $40\u2013$45/month).\n* **Peacock:** While NBC\u2019s streaming service, Peacock, does not have a 24/7 live feed of the main MSNBC channel, a Peacock subscription allows you to watch same-day or next-day on-demand episodes of prime MSNBC shows like *Morning Joe* and *The Rachel Maddow Show*.\n* **NBC News NOW:** If you just want live news coverage, NBC's free, ad-supported 24/7 streaming news channel, **NBC News NOW**, is available to stream for free on Pluto TV, Tubi, Samsung TV Plus, Peacock, and the NBC News app.\n\n*Note: Be cautious of third-party \"free live TV\" websites found on search engines. These unofficial streams are often illegal, violate copyright laws, and are heavily laden with aggressive pop-up ads, redirect loops, and malware risks.*",
